           S.No.               Command                        Description
             1                 `ipconfig`                     Displays the
                                                              system's IP
                                                              address, subnet
                                                              mask, and default
                                                              gateway.

             2                 `ipconfig /all`                Displays complete
                                                              network
                                                              configuration,
                                                              including MAC
                                                              address and DNS
                                                              details.

             3                 `ipconfig /release`            Releases the
                                                              currently assigned
                                                              IP address.

             4                 `ipconfig /renew`              Requests a new IP
                                                              address from the
                                                              DHCP server.

             5                 `ipconfig /flushdns`           Clears the DNS
                                                              resolver cache.

             6                 `ping google.com`              Checks network
                                                              connectivity and
                                                              measures response
                                                              time.

             7                 `ping 127.0.0.1`               Tests the local
                                                              TCP/IP network
                                                              stack using the
                                                              loopback address.

             8                 `tracert google.com`           Displays the route
                                                              taken by packets to
                                                              reach the
                                                              destination.

             9                 `pathping google.com`          Displays the route
                                                              and packet-loss
                                                              information at each
                                                              hop.

             10                `nslookup google.com`          Looks up DNS
                                                              information, such
                                                              as the IP address
                                                              associated with a
                                                              domain name.

             11                `hostname`                     Displays the
                                                              computer's host
                                                              name.

             12                `getmac`                       Displays the MAC
                                                              addresses of
                                                              network adapters.

             13                `arp -a`                       Displays the ARP
                                                              table, which maps
                                                              IP addresses to MAC
                                                              addresses.

             14                `netstat`                      Displays active
                                                              network connections
                                                              and listening
                                                              ports.

             15                `netstat -ano`                 Displays all
                                                              connections,
                                                              listening ports,
                                                              and their
                                                              associated process
                                                              IDs (PIDs).

             16                `route print`                  Displays the
                                                              system's IP routing
                                                              table.

             17                `nbtstat -n`                   Displays local
                                                              NetBIOS names.

             18                `netsh wlan show profiles`     Displays saved
                                                              Wi-Fi network
                                                              profiles.

             19                `netsh wlan show interfaces`   Displays details
                                                              about the current
                                                              Wi-Fi interface and
                                                              connection.

             20                `getmac /v`                    Displays detailed
                                                              MAC address
                                                              information along
                                                              with adapter names.

             21                `ipconfig /displaydns`         Displays the
                                                              contents of the DNS
                                                              resolver cache.

             22                `ping -t google.com`           Continuously sends
                                                              ping requests until
                                                              stopped with
                                                              `Ctrl + C`.

             23                `tracert -d google.com`        Traces the route
                                                              without resolving
                                                              IP addresses into
                                                              hostnames.
